    "long_instructions": "### **Write It Yourself**\r\n\r\n#### **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. **Build:** Make Button Two, when clicked, show this message in the text area: \"Button Two was clicked!\" Add your code without deleting the code for Button One.\r\n\r\n2. **Test:** Click both Button One and Button Two and check that they work as expected.\r\n\r\n3. **Check Code:** Look for where your code:\r\n\r\n   * selects the button\r\n   * adds an event listener\r\n   * listens for a click\r\n   * changes the message\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n:::details [Need help? Ask AI for hints or explanations.]\r\n\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\nIn this level, AI can help you:\r\n\r\n* understand what a line of code does\r\n* remember JavaScript syntax\r\n* suggest what kind of code you need next\r\n\r\nIn this level, AI should **not** write the JavaScript for you.\r\n\r\n**Try asking:**\r\n\r\n* “How do I write a click event listener in JavaScript?”\r\n* “What does `getElementById` do?”\r\n* “How do I change text in JavaScript?”\r\n\r\nIf the answer is confusing, try:\r\n\r\n* “Can you explain this in simpler terms?”\r\n* “Can you give me a hint instead of the answer?”\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n",
