    "teacher_markdown": "## Teaching this Lesson\r\n\r\n:::details  [**Prompting Questions for Students**]\r\n\r\n- How do you grab an element, like a button, from the HTML? Direct students to lines 19 and 20 in `index.html`\r\n- Where in `script.js` should this happen? \r\n- How would you let the user know the button click was successful?\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n## Preparing to Teach\r\n\r\n:::details  [**Walkthrough of the Code**]\r\n\r\n#### **1. Selects the Button**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst buttonTwo = document.getElementById(\"buttonTwo\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis line finds Button Two in the HTML so the program can interact with it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **2. Selects the Text Area**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst textArea = document.getElementById(\"textArea\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis selects the part of the page that will be updated.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **3. Adds an Event Listener**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nbuttonTwo.addEventListener(\"click\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis tells the program to listen for a click on Button Two.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **4. Event Handler (What Runs)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n() => {...}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis function contains the code that runs when the button is clicked.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **5. Updates the Page (Response)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\ntextArea.textContent = \"Button Two was clicked!\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis changes the text on the page when Button Two is clicked.\r\n:::"
